<title>USA: Monsanto jumps to top of NYSE actives.</title>
<headline>Monsanto jumps to top of NYSE actives.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Monsanto Co's stock edged higher and became the most heavily traded issue on the New York Stock Exchange in afternoon trading.</p>
<p>The stock gained 1-3/4 to 39-1/8 on volume of about 4.1 million shares.</p>
<p>The stock got a boost after sinking to $36 to $37 a share -- a level that often draws investors, analysts said.</p>
<p>There have been no changes in the company's fundamentals to account for the share activity, analysts said.</p>
<p>Monsanto also said it did not know of any reason to account for its stock activity.</p>
<p>(( -- Wall Street desk 212-859-1730))</p>
